														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2541006">
									

<p>I feel like there's a way that someone could write a decent article revolving around a modern-day leper colony and the social implications that would have.</p>
<p>This isn't a <em>bad</em> attempt at it, but there's elements of this that kind of feel like it's skimming the surface of the subject material. The D-Class whose perspective informs us of this phenomenon is just misunderstood, and becomes a more agreeable person simply because someone is nice to him for once; that struck me as a little facile. Additionally, the fact that what looks to be a pretty horrific skin condition doesn't cause any sort of concern among the people that have it. In some ways, it might be more interesting if you had a group of people who understood that what they had was a really, really messed up disease, and were bothered by that (as I think any rational person would be), but were glad anyway because the positive aspects of the social interaction outweighed the affliction.</p>

							</div>

								
					
